    "overview": "Find and explain probabilities, make predictions, and work with compound events.",
    "problems": [
      {
        "prompt": "A bag has 5 green, 3 orange and 2 black marbles. Find P(orange) and P(not green)."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Is an event with probability 0.95 likely or unlikely? Give an example of an event with a probability close to 0.95."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A spinner landed on blue 36 times in 120 spins. Estimate the probability of blue, and predict how many times it would land on blue in 500 spins."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A number cube is rolled twice. What is the probability of rolling a 6 both times?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A family has 3 children. Assume a girl or a boy is equally likely each time. List all the outcomes and find the probability of exactly two girls."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Kai says that when you roll two number cubes, a sum of 2 is as likely as a sum of 7, because each is just one sum. Explain why Kai is wrong."
      }
    ],
